    "en": "Captain Tsubasa: Road to 2002 Tokubetsu Hen - F.C.R.B. Stadium Opening Match"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "Captain Tsubasa: Road to 2002 Tokubetsu Hen - F.C.R.B. Stadium Opening Match (キャプテン翼ROAD TO 2002特別編 F.C.R.B. STADIUM OPENING MATCH, Captain Tsubasa: Road to 2002 special story - F.C.R.B. Stadium Opening Match) is a 10-page oneshot story created as a promotional item for the F.C.R.B. Stadium Project exhibition, a work of Japanese architect Nobuo Araki for the fictional team F.C. Real Bristol (or F.C.R.B, also part of a larger project).\n\nThe manga was originally released in Shueisha's Mankaku Vol.39 (an extra edition of the Seinen magazine Weekly Young Jump) cover date #2004-06-05 (on sale starting 2004-04-28). The manga has not been republished so far.\n\nThe manga is a promotional product for the F.C.R.B Project, so it is not part of the canon of the regular series."
  },
